TWO FAILURES OF THE SAME KIND, both mine, both worth remembering.

1. I SHIPPED A CLASS THAT GENERATED NO CSS, AND SAID IT WAS FIXED.
   Last pass set bg-slate-950/92 on the flip-card faces. Tailwind's default
   opacity scale steps by 5, so /92 matches no utility and emitted nothing —
   the faces ended up with NO background, strictly worse than the /50 and /80
   they replaced. I then screenshotted the result and read it as 'much more
   solid'. It was not; I saw what I expected to see.
   This is the SECOND time on this site (bg-black/88 was the first), which means
   knowing the rule was never the gap — checking was. Any non-multiple-of-5
   Tailwind opacity now gets verified against a standalone tailwind build before
   it is called done, and a computed-style read afterwards. Confirmed live this
   time: rgba(2,6,23,0.984).

2. FOUR PALETTES FOR ONE COMPLAINT.
   'I don't like the colours in portfolio' drew three different palettes out of
   me — unrelated hues, a wide neon arc, a narrow cyan->indigo ramp — before the
   user spelled it out: 'Just make everything in experience white/silver.' The
   note never moved because the variable was never WHICH hues; it was whether
   that list should carry hue at all.
   Recurring shape, now seen with club text colour, the portfolio ramp, and name
   brightness: when N attempts at 'pick a better X' all fail, the answer is
   usually 'no X', not 'the N+1th X'. Consider removing the property before
   tuning it again.

